<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander Suvorov</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Suvorov</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander Suvorov was a Russian general of the eighteenth century, famous for never losing a major battle. He won important victories against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, including the storming of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/izmail">Izmail</a> in 1790, and commanded campaigns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. He is regarded as one of the greatest commanders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-suvorov.jpg" alt="Alexander Suvorov" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joseph Kreutzinger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joseph_Kreutzinger_-_Portrait_of_Count_Alexander_Suvorov_-_WGA12281.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
